  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Chapter eight, lesson four."
   ],
   [
    2.057,
    "ATP and energy coupling."
   ],
   [
    4.297,
    "A rechargeable battery stores energy, spends it, and gets charged again."
   ],
   [
    8.893,
    "Inside a cell, something very like that is going on all the time."
   ],
   [
    12.826,
    "Here is our pathway strip again."
   ],
   [
    14.701,
    "Some of its steps run uphill, and they will not go on their own."
   ],
   [
    18.607,
    "This lesson is about the spark that gives them a push."
   ],
   [
    21.81,
    "A cell does three main kinds of work."
   ],
   [
    24.219,
    "Chemical work builds molecules."
   ],
   [
    26.576,
    "Transport work moves substances across membranes."
   ],
   [
    30.169,
    "Mechanical work moves things, like a vesicle on its track."
   ],
   [
    34.245,
    "All three are endergonic, so they need energy."
   ],
   [
    37.422,
    "To pay for them, cells use energy coupling: an exergonic process drives an endergonic one."
   ],
   [
    43.633,
    "And most energy coupling in cells is done by ATP."
   ]
  ]
 },
